this was the moment the explosion  happened in central Istanbul in the  middle of Sunday afternoon video filmed  in the immediate aftermath shows bodies  lying still on the ground and people  shouting to help for the wounded as the  Smoke Clears  it happened near taxim Square on a busy  street one of the main shopping streets  in the city and popular with tourists a  number of foreigners are understood to  have been caught in the explosion  the Turkish president typed Richard  erdogan spoke briefly on National  Television before flying to the G20  leaders Summit in Indonesia  our nation should be sure that the  perpetrators will be punished as they  deserve by uncovering all the elements  that led up to this incident on Easter  Cloud Street  this is the first major terror attack in  Istanbul for five years after Kurdish  militants and Islamic State separately  targeted the city in a series of attacks  between 2015 and 2017.  presidential elections are next year  often a tense time in Turkey  and this attack could harm the tourist  market so vital at the moment with  Turkey's economy in a desperate way  Alistair bunkel Sky News
 

